<item>
<title>U.S. heat deaths undercounted by an order of magnitude</title>
<link>https://newrepublic.com/article/215007/goodbye-least-apocalyptic-summer-rest-life</link>
<description>NPR/Boston University analysis found \~9,000 annual heat-related deaths versus CDC’s official \~700. Unnoticed effect: Florida tallies may be 40 times official figures, distorting public-health budgets and emergency-planning baselines nationwide.</description>
<pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
<guid isPermaLink="false">us-heat-undercount-2026</guid>
